# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for tonight's four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-3 throughout: T1 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after T1's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# T6: hand the cards back to production: the status of every board and the all-four reset. The driver then runs, outside this job
# file, the platform's fabric re-measure, the :latest retag in the rig daemon's local store, and placement through the admin API
# (which needs the user's go-ahead and an admin token); then /v1/models and one chat on the placed production endpoint.
# Re-place tp4-serve-2 (audits on). tp4-serve-3 is placed only if chosen after T1, T4 and its platform replay, which is not in this
# window. Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric re-measure passes, the endpoint answers /v1/models with
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes, and the engine log shows profile c2-packed-tp4 with the audits on. If the reset does not
# heal a board after T5, production stays down until it does: accept that risk before the window.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
